From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:35:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [tests] Add a hardening harness: sanitizers, valgrind and
 static analysis.

tests/hardening/run builds tests/tests.pro from clean in a shadow build
directory and runs every test under ASan+UBSan and TSan, with one or more
compilers, and under valgrind memcheck, failing on any report.
TEST_RUNNER runs a cross build on the build host through a sysroot's
loader.

tests/hardening/static-analysis builds the tree with g++ and clang++
through a wrapper that records the compile commands, then runs gcc
-fanalyzer (-O0 and -O2), clang --analyze with the alpha checkers,
clang-tidy, cppcheck and flawfinder over src/, lib/ and plugins/, and
shellcheck over the scripts run as root at install time. Every -c
compiler (with -q giving that target's qmake) builds the tree with a
strict warning set; link errors are ignored so the plugins can be
checked against header-only dependencies. Findings are compared,
without line numbers, with a baseline in which every accepted finding
has the reason it was accepted, so only new ones fail the run.

sparse is not run, it parses C only and there is no C here; nor is
Coccinelle, whose C++ parser gets through 3 of the 39 sources.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
